# Scope-path semantics — implementation report

## ⚠️ Governance disclosure first

**A parallel process modified and committed to this repository during my run. I did not commit, stage, or push anything.**

- `git reflog` shows `ba80298 fix(harness): honest scope-path semantics -- globs are globs, prose is prose`, authored `AI Assistant <bot@example.com>` at `Mon Sep 14 11:23:51 2026 +0800`.
- That commit contains files I never edited (`.github/instructions/ai-autonomy-escalation.instructions.md`, `.ai/chair-decisions.md`, `.ai/scope-path-semantics.contract.md`, `.ai/builder-spec-truth.contract.md`) and it **excluded my three new test files** — so it is a separate writer.
- It captured the parser/driver/lint at an intermediate point. My working tree adds the final lint change (parser-backed fallback) and the three test files; the parser also carries a concurrent prose-detection refinement I did not originally author (`$backticked` / `$looksLikeProse`). I adopted it because it is in scope, I verified it, and I locked it with tests.

The deliverable is the **working tree**. HEAD `ba80298` plus the uncommitted working-tree changes together contain the complete slice.

