Every difference is explained:

- **False positives removed (11 contracts).** `ai-autonomy-mechanise-doctrine` `[kernel]→0`, `akira-theme-scope` `[migrations,modules]→0`, `p1.3`/`p2.4`/`p3.1`/`p3.1b`/`p3.2`/`p4.2a-r2`/`p6a` `[migrations]→0`, `playwright-rate-limit-cap` `[kernel,modules,src,config,migrations]→0`, and the contract under implementation `scope-path-semantics` `[src,modules,public]→0`. These were all single-segment directory prohibitions whose trailing slash had been stripped. **This is CD-7 fact 3 fixed.**
- **True positives surfaced.** `harness-acceptance-a-simulated-harpp` `0→2` (`` `~/.config/harpp/` `` and `` `git add` `` rules that the old primary path silently dropped). `contract-corpus-conformance` `[kernel]→[`git add` rule]`. `ai-autonomy-remote-shape-repair` `[this]→[this repair., `git add` rule]`. **This is CD-7 fact 1/4 fixed.**
- **`ai-autonomy-harpp-binding`** (parse-FAIL, fallback) `3→5`: the fallback now asks the kernel parser, so it reports the actual prose bullets (`seven files listed above.`, the two `~/.config/...` bullets, `No git add...`, `No weakening...`) instead of bare-word tokens. The fallback and primary now use one rule.

